do Resolve the absolute project. Read branch, HEAD, porcelain status, and active
    Git operation state. Return an object with project, branch, attached_head,
    conflicts, active_operation, and changes_present. as @context

do Verify @context has an attached HEAD, no unresolved conflicts, and no active
    merge, rebase, cherry-pick, or revert.

if @context.changes_present == false
    return "There are no changes to commit."

do Resolve the absolute project and active Jira ticket ID from the explicit
    request or this conversation's task context. Reject a supplied-ID mismatch
    with the active task. Do not infer a task from a temporary filename or search
    for task files. Return an object with project, ticket_id (null if unknown),
    and ticket containing the complete previously loaded Jira object or null. as @task_context

if @task_context.ticket_id == null
    ask "Which Jira ticket should this work use?" as @ticket_input

    do Validate @ticket_input as one Jira ticket ID and return @task_context
        with that ticket_id. as @task_context

set project = @task_context.project
set ticket_id = @task_context.ticket_id
set ticket = @task_context.ticket

do Verify any available @ticket identifies @ticket_id and retain @project,
    @ticket_id, and any complete ticket as this conversation's active task.
    Resolve identity locally; do not call Jira or write task files.

if @ticket == null
    return "Commit requires complete ticket context. Load it with /inux task <id>, then retry."

do Verify @ticket_id is valid, any supplied ID matches it, and
    @context.branch contains the exact case-sensitive ticket token without
    making it part of a longer ID.

do Read complete staged and unstaged diffs plus relevant untracked files.
    Understand what changed using @ticket and code context. Select requested or
    clearly related ticket changes. Return an object with clear, selected
    changes, and excluded changes. as @scope

if @scope.clear == false
    ask "Which changes should be committed, including already staged changes?" as @scope_input

    do Resolve @scope from @scope_input. Return an updated object with clear,
        selected changes, and excluded changes. as @scope

if @scope.clear != true
    return "Commit stopped because the intended change scope is unclear."

do Verify @scope excludes unrelated staged changes and unintended secrets or
    artifacts.

do Group @scope.selected changes by purpose, with dependencies first. Draft one
    commit for related changes and separate commits for independent purposes.
    Every message must be one line <TICKET-ID>: <Capitalized present-tense
    summary> using @ticket_id exactly once, followed by colon and one
    space, with no body or extra prefix. Return an object with ordered groups
    and commit_count. as @commit_plan

do Run only missing repository-required verification for @scope.selected,
    reusing results for unchanged content and keeping repository hooks enabled.
    Return the observed verification results. as @verification

do Verify @verification passed every required check.

set commit_index = 0
set completed_commits = []

repeat @commit_plan.commit_count times
    do Select the group at @commit_index from @commit_plan.groups. Re-read the
        active ticket ID and branch and verify both still match @ticket_id
        and @context.branch. Return the selected group with message, paths, and
        hunks. as @group

    print "Proposed commit message:" @group.message
    ask "Is this commit message good? Reply yes to approve; any other reply stops." as @message_approval

    if @message_approval != "yes"
        return "Commit stopped because the message was not approved."

    do Stage only @group.paths and @group.hunks. Preserve partial staging and
        unrelated work and index entries. Fail if safe separation is impossible.

    run git -C @context.project diff --cached --check as @staged_check

    do Read the full staged diff. Verify it is nonempty, exactly @group,
        covered by @verification, and accurately described by @group.message.

    run git -C @context.project commit -m @group.message as @commit_result

    do Read the created commit SHA and remaining status. Append an object with
        the SHA and @group.message to @completed_commits and return the updated
        array. as @completed_commits

    set commit_index = @commit_index + 1

print Report @completed_commits and any remaining changes. Include completed commits if a later group failed.
